# -*- mode:org;coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: vl-doc-*/VLX-namespace family: BricsCAD V26 provides it, contradicting the multidocument analysis
#+AUTHOR: Pascal J. Bourguignon
#+DATE: 2026-08-09
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: doc
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-vl-doc-namespace-family-bricscad

The multidocument analysis document
(clautolisp-multidocument-analysis.org) classifies ~vl-doc-export~ /
~vl-doc-import~ / ~vl-arx-import~ as existing "under --autocad only"
and says that under ~--bricscad~ they "should signal an
unsupported-feature condition rather than silently degrade".

Reality check on a real BricsCAD V26 (macOS, LispEx 26.0), via the
alpm verification probes (probe V-9, alpm CI job
verify:bricscad:macos, pipeline 2744343498, job 15791433487,
2026-08-09): the WHOLE family is present as SUBRs --
vl-doc-export, vl-doc-import, vl-doc-ref, vl-doc-set, vl-arx-import,
vl-list-exported-functions, vl-list-loaded-vlx, vl-vlx-loaded-p,
vl-unload-vlx, vl-acad-defun, vl-acad-undefun, vl-bb-ref, vl-bb-set.
~(vl-doc-export 'fn)~ executed in the document namespace returns T
(inert success; probe V-7).

This matches the Bricsys V25/V26 DevRef "VLX NameSpace Support"
page: since BricsCAD V18.2 (DEScoder v2.7+), the VLX-NameSpace
feature is supported for DES-encrypted LISP files, and these
functions are listed as supported.

* Suggested fix

- Correct the multidocument analysis (vl-doc-* is NOT AutoCAD-only;
  BricsCAD supports it for DES-encrypted namespace modules).
- The bricscad-* dialects should provide the family (inert T outside
  a namespace module, like the real engine), not signal
  unsupported-feature.

* Triage 2026-08-09 — NO CODE CHANGE NEEDED; docs-only

Verified against the tree at =528578c=: the runtime *already* behaves
the way the probe found the real BricsCAD behaves. All thirteen names
of the family are registered unconditionally in
=clautolisp/autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp= —
VL-ACAD-DEFUN, VL-ACAD-UNDEFUN, VL-ARX-IMPORT, VL-BB-REF, VL-BB-SET,
VL-DOC-EXPORT, VL-DOC-IMPORT, VL-DOC-REF, VL-DOC-SET,
VL-LIST-EXPORTED-FUNCTIONS, VL-LIST-LOADED-VLX, VL-UNLOAD-VLX,
VL-VLX-LOADED-P — and a grep for dialect gating over the whole family
(=dialect= / =unsupported= / =availab= / =autocad-only=) returns
nothing. So the second bullet of the suggested fix is already
satisfied: no dialect signals unsupported-feature, because the family
was never gated in the first place.

What is actually wrong is only the analysis *document*,
=clautolisp/documentation/clautolisp-multidocument-analysis.org=, in
two places:

- line 102, the table row labelling separate-namespace VLX
  "(AutoCAD only)";
- line 311, the prose asserting the family "exist[s] under
  =--autocad=" and should signal unsupported-feature under
  =--bricscad=.

Scope: correct those two passages and cite the probe (alpm job
=verify:bricscad:macos=, pipeline 2744343498, job 15791433487) plus
the Bricsys DevRef "VLX NameSpace Support" page. Docs-only ⇒ no
=version.lisp= bump. Overlaps the VL-DOC-EXPORT section of
=autolisp-spec-alpm-verification-findings.issue= (that one upgrades
the *spec* entries from "presumed compatible" to verified; this one
fixes the *analysis* document) — do them together.
